  data: {
    LLM: 'Players take turns playing cards (or sets) equal to or higher than the top of the pile. If unable or unwilling, they pick up the whole pile. While stock remains, players refill hand back to three cards. Special cards commonly include 2 (wild/reset), 10 (burn pile), and four-of-a-kind pile clear. After hand cards are gone, players use face-up table cards, then unknown face-down cards.',
    Player: 'Players take turns playing cards (or sets) equal to or higher than the top of the pile. If unable or unwilling, they pick up the whole pile. While stock remains, players refill hand back to three cards. Special cards commonly include 2 (wild/reset), 10 (burn pile), and four-of-a-kind pile clear. After hand cards are gone, players use face-up table cards, then unknown face-down cards.',
    objective: 'Get rid of all your cards by playing them to the central pile; play cards equal to or higher than the top card or pick up the whole pile. The last player left holding cards is the loser (the shithead).',
    gameplay: 'Players take turns playing cards (or sets) equal to or higher than the top of the pile. If unable or unwilling, they pick up the whole pile. While stock remains, players refill hand back to three cards. Special cards commonly include 2 (wild/reset), 10 (burn pile), and four-of-a-kind pile clear. After hand cards are gone, players use face-up table cards, then unknown face-down cards.',
    keyRules: [
      'Failing to play requires taking the entire pile.',
      '10 and certain quartet conditions clear the pile in common rulesets.',
      'Last player with remaining cards is the loser.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
