    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Get rid of all your cards by playing them to the central pile; play cards equal to or higher than the top card or pick up the whole pile. The last player left holding cards is the loser (the shithead).',
      'Turn-flow example: Players take turns playing cards (or sets) equal to or higher than the top of the pile. If unable or unwilling, they pick up the whole pile. While stock remains, players refill hand back to three cards. Special cards commonly include 2 (wild/reset), 10 (burn pile), and four-of-a-kind pile clear. After hand cards are gone, players use face-up table cards, then unknown face-down cards.',
      'Scoring example: Shithead is usually placement-based rather than point-based: players go out in order, and the last remaining player loses. Do not finish last; the final player left with cards is the loser..',
